title: Welcome Aboard
files:
  - .assets/img-100-01-01.png
  - .assets/img-100-01-02.png
  - em.prog:em.examples.basic/Ex01_HelloP.em.ts
  - em.prog:em.examples.basic/Ex02_BlinkerP.em.ts

steps:

  - cmds:
    text: |

      {[ht,$start]Welcome Aboard}

      This initial tour has two primary objectives:

      {[bi,arrow_circle_right]} Learning how to use the **TOUR GUIDE**.

      {[bi,arrow_circle_right]} Tweaking the UI to remove some visual clutter.

      To proceed through the current tour, you'll use the five buttons across the top of this view:

      {[bm,1]} **Back** &ndash; go to the previous stop on this tour<br>
      {[bm,2]} **Next** &ndash; go to the next stop on this tour<br>
      {[bm,3]} **Refresh** &ndash; replay the current stop on this tour<br>
      {[bm,4]} **Restart** &ndash; rewind to the first stop on this tour <br>
      {[bm,5]} **End** &ndash; stop this tour and close the **TOUR GUIDE**<br>

      Click the **Next** button to continue with **Tour&thinsp;01**&thinsp;....

  - cmds:
      - view 1
    text: |

      {[ht,household_supplies]Tidying up &ndash; Activity Bar}

      You can remove some extraneous elements from the **Activity Bar** at the left of the **VS Code** window.

      Right-click inside the **Activity Bar** and uncheck the items suggested in the screenshot.

      We also moved the **EM&bull;Browser** and **EM&bull;Tours** activities to the top and bottom &ndash; for easy reference.

      {[in]To zoom in&thinsp;&middot;&thinsp;out within the image's editor tab, press <b>Ctrl</b> (or <b>Cmd</b>) while scrolling your mouse down&thinsp;&middot;&thinsp;up.}
      
      Suggestions only &ndash; click **Next** and let's keep moving&thinsp;....

  - cmds:
      - close 1
      - view 2
    text: |

      {[ht,household_supplies]Tidying up &ndash; Outline View}

      You should place the **Outline View** in the **Secondary Side Bar** &ndash; even if it has nothing to show.

      The **Outline View** proves invaluable once we start exploring some **EM&bull;Script** source code.

      {[bm,1]} select **View > Open View** from the main menu<br>
      {[bm,2]} type `Outline` to locate then `<ENTER>` to open<br>
      {[bm,3]} drag the **OUTLINE** tab to the **Secondary Side Bar**<br>
      {[bm,4]} drop the **OUTLINE** tab just below **CHAT**<br>

      Again, suggestions only &ndash; click **Next** to continue&thinsp;....

  - cmds:
      - close 2
      - open 3
    focus: [3,1]
    text: |

        {[ht,front_hand]Hello EM&bull;Script}

        Going forward, most of the tours you'll take will involve examining individual **EM&bull;Script** source files.

        In this case, we've shown you the **EM&bull;Script** source file `Ex01_HelloP.em.ts` within a readonly editor tab.

        {[in]We'll start using '<b>EMS</b>' as shorthand for <b>EM&bull;Script</b>. }

        Even if you've never seen **EMS** code before, you can probably guess what the {[cu]HelloP} program does&thinsp;!!

        Let's dive in&thinsp;....

  - cmds:
      - mark 3 A 2
      - mark 3 B 5
    focus: [3,1]
    acts: ['$reveal']
    text: |

        {[ht,$details]%[cu]HelloP% &ndash; details}

        Many tour-stops will examine a particular source file in greater detail.

        As needed, we'll add lettered "bookmarks" to these files along with corresponding commetary:

        <div class="em-bmlist">

        {[bm,A]} Boilerplate found in all **EMS** files

        {[bm,B]} Note the somewhat unusual {[cd]printf} syntax.

        </div>

        You can also use the {[cb,target]} *action button* to reveal this file within the **EM&bull;Browser** content hiearchy.

        And now, let's execute this **EMS** program&thinsp;....

  - cmds:
    focus: [3,1]
    acts: [$build]
    text: |

        {[ht,$build]%[cu]HelloP% &ndash; build&thinsp;+&thinsp;load}

        Tours focused on specific **EMS** programs will include a **build&thinsp;+&thinsp;load** stop for running this code on target HW.

        For now, we'll rely upon a **Raspberry Pi Pico** simulator (supported by the **Wokwi** extension) as our target.

        If you haven't done so already, follow the **Request a Wowki Key** link on the **EM&bull;Home** editor tab.

        When ready, click the {[cb,build]} *action button* to initiate **build&thinsp;+&thinsp;load** of our {[cu]HelloP} program.

        A **Wokwi Simulator** tab will open in the editor &ndash; with `hello world` output seen in a **Wokwi Terminal** pane.

        Close the **Wokwi Simulator** tab before clicking **Next**.

  - cmds:
    - open 4
    focus: [4,1]
    acts: [$build, $reveal]
    text: |

        {[ht,$build]%[cu]BlinkerP% &ndash; build&thinsp;+&thinsp;load}

        While some **EMS** programs will rely upon{[cd]printf} out&shy;put, many more will simply blink LEDs as their UI.

        To that end, glance at the {[cu]BlinkerP} program shown here.&thinsp; Then click {[cb,build]} and enjoy the show&thinsp;!!

        Over time, you'll run **EMS** programs on a growing list of target platforms featuring a wide range of MCUs.

        Before moving on, click the {[em]%[ci,circuit-board]%&thinsp;Board} status item at the bottom of the **VS Code** window for a preview.

  - cmds:
    text: |

        {[ht,$steps]Next steps}

        Congratulations on completing your first tour.&thinsp;🎉

        After you **End** this tour by clicking the red square, we'll show the **EM&bull;TOURS** view in the **Primary Side Bar**.

        From here, proceed to the next tour in the **Orientation** bundle by clicking (once) on **Content Hierarchy**.

        And after completing **Content Hierarchy** and then **Language Surface**, have fun with the **Basic Examples**.

        {[hc]}


